# The exact libprojectM commit both installers build against.
#
# Not a tag, because there is no release that has what we need. Upstream's
# newest tag is v4.1.7 and the API added since -- user sprites, the texture
# load callback, the log callback -- exists only on master, where CMakeLists
# declares 4.2.0 with no tag to go with it. So the pin is a SHA.
#
# Verified against this commit before it was written down: every one of the 47
# exported declarations in v4.1.0 is byte-identical on master (68 total, so it
# is purely additive), the glibc floor of a container build is unchanged at
# 2.35, and the app played 60 presets on it with no errors.
#
# It also carries the rendering fixes from the whole 4.1.x line that 4.1.0
# predates: inverted Y and wrong angle passed to per-pixel expressions, warp
# shader texel drift, a null dereference in the texture sampler, sampler
# keywords misparsed inside shader comments, and several HLSL transpiler gaps.
# That is the reason to move even before anything binds the new API.
#
# Both installers refuse to build from a source tree that is not at this
# commit, rather than quietly producing a library from whatever was lying
# around. Bump this line to move; the scripts will tell you what to do.
